    "script": "Jesus prays in the garden with sorrow unto death. He asks that the cup pass, yet submits fully: \"Not as I will, but as You will.\" He finds the disciples sleeping and calls them to watch and pray. He accepts the Passion in perfect trust.\n\nIn Gethsemane, Jesus embraces the Father's will in agony, teaching obedience under suffering.\n\nStay with this mystery as you pray.",
    "script_sha256": "763727faec324bc882ccde47b0967c719c9b17a494d203aa70bb6458722e2b2a",
    "source_scripture": "Matthew 26:36-46; Luke 22:43-44",
